# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# CSP is strict on purpose and it is CHEAP here: a source audit of all seven
# games found zero inline event handlers, zero eval, zero new Function, and zero
# Workers — MV3 already forbade all of that, so the games were written without
# them. Bloom Rush's two inline <script> blocks are extracted to a file at build
# time so it does not need a carve-out either.
#
# connect-src names every third-party destination explicitly and no more:
#   api.groq.com                       Veilfall's optional Tier 2 AND Planet Express
#                                      Lounge's default provider — both called with
#                                      the VISITOR'S own key, never a shipped one
#   openrouter.ai                      Planet Express Lounge, alternate provider
#   generativelanguage.googleapis.com  Planet Express Lounge, Gemini provider
#   api.elevenlabs.io                  Planet Express Lounge, optional premium TTS
#   api.playhtml.fun                   the sync socket behind the arcade's shared
#                                      play counts and star ratings (playhtml is
#                                      BUNDLED from npm, not loaded from a CDN, so
#                                      script-src stays 'self')
# Pinning them means a future dependency cannot quietly add another.
#
# WHY THIS WIDENING IS NOT FREE, AND WHY IT IS STILL NARROW.
# This origin holds visitor-supplied API keys in localStorage. Every host added
# here is a host that prompt-injected model output could be talked into POSTing
# a key to. Four were added at once for Planet Express Lounge, which quadrupled
# that surface in a single commit. Three mitigations, all asserted by gates:
#   1. The list is an allowlist, not a wildcard. No `https:` and no subdomain
#      wildcards — `api.groq.com`, not `*.groq.com`.
#   2. scripts/verify-llm-egress.mjs proves the pin BLOCKS an exfiltration fetch
#      to an unlisted host, with a listed host as the positive control. A pin
#      nobody proved is just a comment.
#   3. Keys are per-visitor and per-browser. There is no shipped key to steal;
#      the worst case is a visitor losing their own key, which is why the app
#      says so at the point of entry rather than in a policy page.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://api.groq.com https://openrouter.ai https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com https://api.elevenlabs.io https://api.playhtml.fun wss://api.playhtml.fun; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Game code is versioned by deploy, not by filename, so it must revalidate.
# Getting this wrong is how a player ends up running half of yesterday's build.
/games/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/shared/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
